** Things to Note **
Again, minimal AI was used for this Lab and writing its associated queries.
Gemini was only used for debugging purposes e.g. SELECT or JOIN errors caused by bad query syntax or unintended behavior.
This was a pretty good assignment for understanding how primary keys and foreign keys interact with each other,
particularly within the constraints of the assignment sheet (e.g. pulling payloads with a certain name or numeric value).
I also got to learn how to make more detailed queries from this assignment. Class teaches us the basics like "SELECT FROM WHERE"
but not how to make detailed queries in practice, which is where this homework comes into play. I also learned how subqueries work
and that they don't inherit the FROM properties of the query they're nested under. Plenty learned today, plenty to learn tomorrow.
Looking forward to doing more in this class!

- Alex
